      "description": "DiskCache.Builder().directory(context.cacheDir.resolve(\"image_cache\")) passes a java.io.File where Coil 3 requires okio.Path; compile error, occurs twice.",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "reasoning": "Verified in the file. The two occurrences are at lines 115 (.directory(context.cacheDir.resolve(\"image_cache\"))) and 136 (.directory(androidContext().cacheDir.resolve(\"image_cache\"))) - the finding cited 116/137, off by one, but the code is present. context.cacheDir is a java.io.File and File.resolve(String) is a Kotlin stdlib extension returning File. Coil 3's DiskCache.Builder.directory() takes okio.Path with no File overload (Coil moved to okio for multiplatform; the Coil 2 File signature was dropped). Kotlin performs no implicit File->Path conversion, so this is a genuine type-mismatch compile error against the declared coil3 3.0.4. The finding's supporting point is also accurate: the file DID adopt the Coil 3 MemoryCache API (no-arg MemoryCache.Builder() + maxSizePercent(context, 0.25) at lines 108-109), making the File-based directory call an unconverted Coil 2 signature. CONFIRMED (line numbers 115/136, not 116/137)."
