      "description": "ImageLoader.Builder(context).respectCacheHeaders(true) is a Coil 2 method removed from ImageLoader.Builder in Coil 3.",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
      "reasoning": "Verified at line 119, chained on ImageLoader.Builder(context) (block lines 105-120). respectCacheHeaders(Boolean) was an ImageLoader.Builder method in Coil 2. In Coil 3, HTTP handling moved out of the core ImageLoader into the separate network artifacts (coil-network-okhttp / coil-network-ktor), and cache-header behavior is now controlled via CacheStrategy on the network fetcher factory; respectCacheHeaders was removed from ImageLoader.Builder. Calling it on ImageLoader.Builder in coil3 3.0.4 is an undefined method -> compile error. The finding hedged this as 'plausible/version-dependent'; I am confident it is a real removal for Coil 3, so CONFIRMED at minor severity."
    },
    {
      "description": "iOS CachedAsyncImage .task catch swallows all errors (including cancellation) with only a '// log error' comment, then unconditionally sets isLoading=false.",
      "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
